 "background": "Two young lovers are kept apart by the girl's disapproving parents. She bleaches linen on the banks of the Vardar, the river that runs through the middle of Macedonia. It is sung across the Balkans, in North Macedonia, Bulgaria, Greek Macedonia and former Yugoslavia, and is probably the most-covered Macedonian song. *Mori* and *dušo* are endearments, roughly \"hey girl\" and \"my soul\". The song is short and plain, which is much of its power.",
